# Real iCE40 (device "384") chipdb — a CELL-TO-CELL routing slice, verbatim from Project IceStorm.
# Generated by `icebox_chipdb.py -3`; every .net and .buffer block below is copied byte-for-byte from the
# full device chipdb (nets 39/1057/1121 and the two complete `.buffer` mux blocks that drive nets 1057 and
# 1121 at tile (1,1)). It is a real intra-tile connection: logic cell 0's output (net 39 = lutff_0/out)
# reaches logic cell 5's input pin 1 (net 1121 = lutff_5/in_1) through the local track local_g0_0 (net 1057),
# via two real buffer pips. Each mux lists its full 16 source options — of those, only the one whose source
# wire is in this slice connects (the other 15 reference wires outside the slice and are EXCLUDED when the
# routing graph is built, which is itself exercised by the tests). The full chipdb is ~2 MB and is NOT vendored.
